# L §5.16 A random number of items (LOAD-RANDOM where load sees the draw's support exceed the index; tally 2.1.6,
# issue #75): nd = discrete(1 for k in big) draws big's keys, up to 5, past slots' last key 3, so the reality is
# refused at load whatever the asks. tally 2.1.5's refcore didn't see discrete's keys and refused only q_draw's
# path at run (RUN-KEY). T's held basic/random-slots; the engine's bytes.
=== base.tally
model basic
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T's base for M0's load-code fixtures (invented): it loads clean; each fixture of codes/m0/edits.tsv changes one line"

source card "T's fixture card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index qs = [q1, q2]

index slots = int 1..3

index big = int 1..5

input amt: money PLN

input day: date

input xs[s in slots]: money PLN

input rate[k in qs]: num

def fee[k in qs]: money PLN
  rule base v card_2026 = round(amt * rate[k], minor(PLN), half-up)
  rule waived beats base v card_2026 = 0 PLN when rate[k] == 0

def total: money PLN = sum(fee[k] for k in qs)

def nd: dist = discrete(1 for k in big)

def drawn: money PLN = sum(xs[s] for s in 1 .. nd step 1)

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee[q1]

ask q: total, bal(konto, 2026-12-31)

ask q_draw: mean(drawn) paths 10 seed 1

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "the card"
  day = 2026-02-10 "the card"
  xs[1] = 1.00 PLN "the card"
  xs[2] = 2.00 PLN "the card"
  xs[3] = 3.00 PLN "the card"
  rate[q1] = 0.1 "the card"
  rate[q2] = 0 "the card"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
=== expect q
refused: LOAD-RANDOM the draw nd can exceed the last slot of slots (base.tally:34)
